# Summary: imperative, capitalised, no full stop, <= 50 chars
# -----------------------------------------------|
#
# Body: what and why, not how. Wrap at 72 chars.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------|
#
# 50/72 Guide  (tbaggery, 2008):
#
# - Summary of 50 characters or less; it is what `git log --oneline`,
#   `git shortlog`, rebase and email subjects show.
# - Write it in the imperative present tense: "Fix bug", not "Fixed
#   bug" or "Fixes bug" -- it matches the messages git itself writes
#   for merges and reverts.
# - Capitalise the summary and leave off the trailing full stop.
# - Separate summary from body with a blank line; tools such as
#   rebase and format-patch rely on it.
# - Wrap the body at 72 characters, so `git log` stays readable in an
#   80-column terminal after git indents it by four.
# - Separate further paragraphs with blank lines.
# - Bullet points are fine: a hyphen or asterisk, a single space, and
#   a hanging indent, with blank lines between them.
# - Explain what changed and why; the diff already shows how.
